        <p class="blog_content-p">In the article I did about wokeness and the Wheel of Time, I brought up the casting for another movie, set in an African setting, but fantasy, Children of Blood and Bone. I notice that the casting for that, not racially diverse. All the actors, writers, directors, black. Now, this would make sense. I actually applaud this because it should be that way for the casting. I would not like it to be anything other than how the book was. But if every movie, story, TV show, set in a White, European cultural setting needs to be diversified, why should we not expect that when the cultural setting is non-White? I know why, but people do not want to say it. This is about tearing down White culture.</p>

